e{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{8}\\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}(2\\pi -\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-9(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))+\\frac{9}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\pi }{8}-9+\\frac{9}{8}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\pi -72}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529113 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529113 #edb/ref 1069 "q-9640" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529113 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529113 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7c/7ca646111a7708da96fa1bea8aca056abf0c45f9a4295e2beb27181d704aa814.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{8},$ as shown above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529113 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c7bf914-2de6-57ee-85dd-b40dcc8d6cfc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529113 #edb/ref 1074 "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}-\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorna